{"id": "clm:3a57072070b5d5e13ba49a84e6682c1a973918132154b675b6c412033f1ce1be", "type": "statement", "text": "The Agent MongoDB check supports custom find, count and aggregate metrics. Database Monitoring adds query snapshots, slow-query metrics, execution plans and collection insights beyond the standard integration. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-23)", "source_url": "https://github.com/DataDog/integrations-core/blob/master/mongo/README.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Datadog Integration"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:29931662f9c71e5bd8c1778e8f26a537e758a4aa830f36bb23dfe7b1a2f300ec", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:958cea4f6aaa3747976a2e0ec48793f3f731f3722ce0b4b29a7251ecefb9eae4"]}
{"id": "clm:5227ce9016ca31aee3e86dccb872837f2f9d633e826b68acb7091945e45021fd", "type": "statement", "text": "Datadog's standard MongoDB integration distinguishes Database Monitoring as an additional product for query snapshots, slow-query metrics, database load and execution plans. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-23)", "source_url": "https://github.com/DataDog/integrations-core/blob/master/mongo/README.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Datadog Integration"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:29931662f9c71e5bd8c1778e8f26a537e758a4aa830f36bb23dfe7b1a2f300ec", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:68f108400d0cd20f45664a923d01fdac43f346a110fc68ec3e24af555f84f04c"]}
{"id": "clm:c88a360f491cfe8df209a3bf68942e4e755e51ef6482ad220bb653dffd1ebfb9", "type": "statement", "text": "Atlas provides cluster, replica-set and database tags on relevant metrics. Custom tags require opt-in and apply to metrics rather than alerts. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-14)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/tutorial/datadog-integration.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Datadog Integration"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:29931662f9c71e5bd8c1778e8f26a537e758a4aa830f36bb23dfe7b1a2f300ec", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:e40d86739e3ac8800bc9f1fb2cc9f92656f26a40a1e33ba4a8b40ad997f4eb15"]}
{"id": "clm:9f90281567d92946f41bb70d9622766d08125dcd99efafea3785e7b6749afed1", "type": "statement", "text": "Atlas warns that mongodb.atlas.replstatus.health can remain healthy when nodes stop sending pings, or become inaccurate during partitions and Datadog ingestion problems. Configure no-data monitoring rather than treating health=1 alone as proof of availability. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/tutorial/datadog-integration.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Datadog Integration"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:29931662f9c71e5bd8c1778e8f26a537e758a4aa830f36bb23dfe7b1a2f300ec", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:7803bfff458e090daa31744c8c8fb63eb1562675d65db891050b1e92253461df", "ev:9cd78c2ad4055f7533f03e96bc2f7a3a118cae53780c2e9c7a843ae8f9e90fa1"]}
{"id": "clm:aa21fc65d3ebc3dc534b1aaa357045484ce585e61a290f6619806c76b4ea24e4", "type": "statement", "text": "Atlas exposes organization, project, cluster and database tags. User-defined resource tags are optional and apply to metrics rather than alerts. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-14)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/tutorial/datadog-integration.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Datadog Integration"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://docs.datadoghq.com/integrations/mongodb-atlas/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:29931662f9c71e5bd8c1778e8f26a537e758a4aa830f36bb23dfe7b1a2f300ec", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:e40d86739e3ac8800bc9f1fb2cc9f92656f26a40a1e33ba4a8b40ad997f4eb15"]}
{"id": "clm:b476da6484f173accc14dd1ba04148acdac5530037db788c8f84f875dbc313f6", "type": "statement", "text": "Atlas pushes metrics into Datadog; setup uses a Datadog API key in Atlas project integrations. Both vendors document an M10+ cluster requirement. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-14)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/tutorial/datadog-integration.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Datadog Integration"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://docs.datadoghq.com/integrations/mongodb-atlas/", "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/cli/current/command/atlas-integrations-create-DATADOG.md", "https://github.com/DataDog/integrations-core/blob/master/mongo/README.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:29931662f9c71e5bd8c1778e8f26a537e758a4aa830f36bb23dfe7b1a2f300ec", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:6a25e22215c96da5496429266332ea0b00b92d63e0d3082152afbcf708b1201e", "ev:a6cfab37f0bf14b1beaefa593574c08c5968d6e974c4d09272af2d61c1bd6bfe"]}
{"id": "clm:19f88609b7aa3ca51f5b147d144dee4326753e8a1eadb073fca35e80eaec76ca", "type": "statement", "text": "Atlas setup requires a Datadog API key. The CLI command atlas integrations create DATADOG creates or updates the project integration. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/tutorial/datadog-integration.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Datadog Integration"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/cli/current/command/atlas-integrations-create-DATADOG.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:29931662f9c71e5bd8c1778e8f26a537e758a4aa830f36bb23dfe7b1a2f300ec", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:6aae9ce7cc4e4e9c0cc92c73fed166ea1f67bf1760cdf470a899c3d79039490d"]}
{"id": "clm:00edd73c1f63c9a4f429204ef48730cc8b587085ecca516eae0fd99eb45de20d", "type": "statement", "text": "Atlas can deliver alerts as Datadog events through the same integration used for project metrics. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/tutorial/datadog-integration.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Datadog Integration"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://docs.datadoghq.com/integrations/mongodb-atlas/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:29931662f9c71e5bd8c1778e8f26a537e758a4aa830f36bb23dfe7b1a2f300ec", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:1979ca41d8dafe4c2e58ba43fa0b7a0f42043cb8a164d02875aca96712ca25ce", "ev:4099003c228a566006456eab50c29f37247d6fe37c41cfdbf5f70e04bda65f90"]}
{"id": "clm:734378519cfbf43808067567c1c2aef70bd31d0fe79185b1d1031622f55ff139", "type": "statement", "text": "Atlas disables high-cardinality database, collection-latency and query-shape metric exports by default; enable sendDatabaseMetrics, sendCollectionLatencyMetrics and sendQueryShapeMetrics explicitly. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-14)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/tutorial/datadog-integration.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Datadog Integration"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://docs.datadoghq.com/integrations/mongodb-atlas/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:29931662f9c71e5bd8c1778e8f26a537e758a4aa830f36bb23dfe7b1a2f300ec", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:0847e0aedec65bfd2a67da22ef2b2b757232e2e1fc0b7d4e1682e7ea8e090dd7"]}
{"id": "clm:70934953591a3ecf9356b2aa3d2769ae172c9190918873f89c3a927e929eb798", "type": "statement", "text": "The MongoDB check ships with the Datadog Agent. Its configuration uses mongo.d/conf.yaml and a monitoring user with clusterMonitor plus read permissions for the databases being monitored. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-23)", "source_url": "https://github.com/DataDog/integrations-core/blob/master/mongo/README.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Datadog Integration"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://oneuptime.com/blog/post/2026-03-31-mongodb-monitor-mongodb-with-datadog/view"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:29931662f9c71e5bd8c1778e8f26a537e758a4aa830f36bb23dfe7b1a2f300ec", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:95661baba29681612feefb2ca3ed2393292f2588fe39c778b7bf7704866c86cb", "ev:a6454f0cefd2e895cc49e60d3fcea98297ca74695f55f2ac37575a3209c8aa50"]}
{"id": "clm:a105eb2ea4317dbf06f94e8936a2022e6245b5989f1c023a753b91b2856e7f97", "type": "statement", "text": "MongoDB APM requires instrumentation in the application making database requests. OneUptime illustrates initializing Node.js dd-trace before importing the MongoDB client; installing the database metric check alone does not establish application tracing. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://github.com/DataDog/integrations-core/blob/master/mongo/README.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Datadog Integration"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://oneuptime.com/blog/post/2026-03-31-mongodb-monitor-mongodb-with-datadog/view"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:29931662f9c71e5bd8c1778e8f26a537e758a4aa830f36bb23dfe7b1a2f300ec", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:436f301b3e2d7364dfd60375f04fdeb548da4c68d6577bda506d571ec1716e19", "ev:4cc92f05da0708cedada0849c3e59434ad4b587405b48ea5fa5e164d992d641c"]}
{"id": "clm:e9d504d0e8a118d026c2267cb6aba2e2c10016edbf5777310e2c88b030f94205", "type": "statement", "text": "The Agent integration collects low-level metrics per mongod node, while higher-level collection/index statistics require topology-aware placement. Datadog documents separate replica-set and sharded-cluster layouts. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://github.com/DataDog/integrations-core/blob/master/mongo/README.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Datadog Integration"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:29931662f9c71e5bd8c1778e8f26a537e758a4aa830f36bb23dfe7b1a2f300ec", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:d3a4ba983103823e38538bc05c6d34ad8feb049cc8db77c3938885f00028c21c"]}
{"id": "clm:bc5bf582dee6310e6f1d72da63f5d2f0aeadfda8b9e8dabe3ea47bd88b05b17d", "type": "statement", "text": "The MongoDB integration changelog records safeguards against monitoring overhead and failures: skipping explain on $mergeCursors pipelines to prevent potential crashes, and removing queryStats server-side sorting to avoid sort-memory failures. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-07-08)", "source_url": "https://github.com/DataDog/integrations-core/blob/master/mongo/CHANGELOG.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Datadog Integration"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:29931662f9c71e5bd8c1778e8f26a537e758a4aa830f36bb23dfe7b1a2f300ec", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:428920c35efb5b74a83d6379ae71b96155b8c07b9c822bc42ce0b12bdcb8e69b", "ev:50f1ececb9d2a5190c6313b3f74d48180fce4bfac2528edc45d70dd9fe85e994"]}
{"id": "clm:b9117b07f5c8999c252673fe6a5382ee2288b27bf9f3d8336fbe35a2a29881bc", "type": "statement", "text": "A February 2023 Terraform user reported INTEGRATION_FIELDS_INVALID and INVALID_ENUM_VALUE errors while configuring Datadog region values through the Atlas API. The captured thread records differing Atlas and Terraform documentation values and no follow-up confirming a fix. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/community/forums/t/integration-fields-invalid-error-from-atlas-api-when-trying-to-enable-datadog-integration/214371", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Datadog Integration"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:29931662f9c71e5bd8c1778e8f26a537e758a4aa830f36bb23dfe7b1a2f300ec", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:8a6d4dda93816616385baf54506b5ef60c9ccfd34a6ed9725803bc8cef205ced"]}
{"id": "clm:1489340cc3860ca0ca5cb00f4105df649345e99b1cc3f13502f6f0eb3d45ceaa", "type": "statement", "text": "A Datadog-authored Chef guest post shows automated Agent deployment and configuration of the MongoDB integration through Chef roles; this remains vendor-origin evidence. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.chef.io/blog/datadog-x-chef-how-and-why-these-two-platforms-go-together", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Datadog Integration"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:29931662f9c71e5bd8c1778e8f26a537e758a4aa830f36bb23dfe7b1a2f300ec", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:7d428eb02603c16a57a45b9d4422deb8367deca0c49713a1c36c7fec27d7366d"]}
{"id": "clm:9f38f97c53ea63326aa5ef706c15214388053a087269ee60955a8b3195449ce1", "type": "statement", "text": "Atlas requires Project Owner access for this integration; an Organization Owner must first add themselves to the project with that role. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-14)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/tutorial/datadog-integration.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Datadog Integration"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:29931662f9c71e5bd8c1778e8f26a537e758a4aa830f36bb23dfe7b1a2f300ec", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:a44685fd1c22bbc6e4262a6281c083b6cab4cc0a1c044f9b9312c6d6a00340c4"]}
{"id": "clm:b13ba9c5d69a39b5112d5576834d24d3d78e9a98e0edb0146e554ac527ba62ec", "type": "statement", "text": "Datadog recommends an Agent on each replica-set host, connecting to its local member. Low-level metrics require collection from every mongod, while higher-level collection/index statistics should be collected once. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://github.com/DataDog/integrations-core/blob/master/mongo/README.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Datadog Integration"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:29931662f9c71e5bd8c1778e8f26a537e758a4aa830f36bb23dfe7b1a2f300ec", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:7e4bceca63bc53868027623b144489aeaf8179897812aa040911472e6f564bd5"]}
{"id": "clm:f3cb5ee838c401aceb006b33da23f7f8e325032883049b74d93989df0b584e6d", "type": "statement", "text": "MongoDB logs require a separate Agent configuration: enable logs_enabled in datadog.yaml and configure the MongoDB log source. Log collection is disabled by default. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-23)", "source_url": "https://github.com/DataDog/integrations-core/blob/master/mongo/README.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Datadog Integration"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:29931662f9c71e5bd8c1778e8f26a537e758a4aa830f36bb23dfe7b1a2f300ec", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:b41f8c4e35e8b248397acc8a400a745349614bde461edcabd467d5c8fd38890f"]}
